  "body": "Was told to move this suggestion https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/1289 here, so here it goes\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSometimes you need to validate against a server to check if something already exist\r\n\r\nIt would be nice if the submit event could stall until customValidation has resolved a promise\r\n\r\n```js\r\nvar username = document.querySelector(\"#username\")\r\n\r\nusername.setCustomValidity(\r\n  getUser(username.value).then(user => user ? \"already taken\" : \"\")\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnother idea is from service worker\r\n\r\nHaving `event.waitUntil` on the submit event could maybe also work. when the promise is finally resolved and the form is still valid continue the submit process or show the popups validations message and automatically focus to the first invalid input\r\n\r\nThe problem is that there is no easy way to show the popup message\r\nBut I found a roundabout way https://stackoverflow.com/questions/15467484/async-html5-validation",
